      "topic": "Financial Statements & Ratio Analysis",
      "fact": "The balance sheet is a statement prepared for showing the financial position of the business summarising its assets and liabilities at a given date. It is also called Position Statement. The assets reflect debit balances and liabilities (including capital) reflect credit balances. It is prepared at the end of the accounting period after the trading",
